> [ a number of questions, mostly answered well by others already ]
> -If I've understood you correctly, the clear potion is ALWAYS plain
> water? What is plain water good for?
> -What is holy water good for?

The clear potion is always water of some sort, not necessarily "plain".
Blessed water is holy water. Cursed water is unholy water. Uncursed water
is plain water.

Holy and unholy water are mostly useful for manipulating the BUC status
of items, though they have other auxilliary uses.

Plain water can dilute (stacks of) other potions, and blank scrolls
and spellbooks. (Generally a waste of a good potion, though, as there
are other ways to do this.)

> -What does "Beware, fullmoon tonight!" indicate?

It means you aren't playing vanilla nethack 3.4.x.

The two moon-related messages are "You are lucky!  Full moon tonight."
and "Be careful!  New moon tonight."

Others upthread have nicely explained full moon effects. They say that
cocktrice (sing. "cockatrix" ?) are vastly more dangerous under a new
moon. Rumor has it that new moons being bad luck is just a rumor.

